Linaro xen-vhost-frontend a1e333c5, as DomD's ioreq server for DomZ's virtio-can and
virtio-rng (xenvm/run.sh can). Applied by xenvm/scripts/build-can.sh. Each change, and
where it stands upstream:

- can and rng in the device tables .......... vireshk/xen-vhost-frontend#10
  https://github.com/vireshk/xen-vhost-frontend/pull/10 (needs vireshk/vhost#37)
- answer reads of DriverFeatures ............ #5  https://github.com/vireshk/xen-vhost-frontend/pull/5
  Zephyr's virtio_mmio read-modify-writes this write-only register; failing the
  ioreq left the guest vCPU waiting forever.
- negotiate features on FEATURES_OK ......... #6  https://github.com/vireshk/xen-vhost-frontend/pull/6
  Zephyr's virtio-entropy never writes DriverFeatures selector 0.
- log ioreq errors .......................... #8  https://github.com/vireshk/xen-vhost-frontend/pull/8
- kick from userspace, and no kernel ioeventfd (single ioreq consumer)
  #7 https://github.com/vireshk/xen-vhost-frontend/pull/7 covers the kick only.
  With privcmd's ioeventfd, the kernel and this thread both take ioreqs from the
  same event channel without an atomic claim, and the kernel marks every write
  ioreq INPROCESS while it looks for a QUEUE_NOTIFY. A notify could be lost (the
  guest's buffers are never seen), and an ioreq could be completed twice: Xen then
  logs "device model set bad IO state 3" and injects a data abort into the guest.
  Both seen under host load (campaign 2026-10-23). This patch registers no
  ioeventfd, so this thread is the only consumer and kicks every QUEUE_NOTIFY.
- Cargo.toml [patch] + Cargo.lock: build against the patched vireshk/vhost and
  xen-sys clones (siblings in the build tree), --locked.

The running in a driver domain (xenstore socket, see harness/xs-sock-relay.py) and
the Xen 4.22 domctl version are vireshk/xen-vhost-frontend#9
https://github.com/vireshk/xen-vhost-frontend/issues/9 and mathieupoirier/xen-sys#2.

